course: dictionary
lesson: 9336
title: One word, many meanings: spinner
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word spinner is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. The clues tell you which one fits.
explain: «A salad spinner flings the water outward and off the leaves through the holes.» Here a spinner is a kitchen tool. The words salad, leaves and water are the clues, so it must be a machine that spins things very fast.
explain: In cricket, a spinner is a bowler who makes the ball spin, so it turns in the air or off the ground. A fidget spinner is a small toy you spin on your finger. «Use a fidget spinner or small toy in class only if the teacher allows it.» Whenever you meet spinner, ask: what is spinning, and why?
fact: A spinner is a thing that spins, such as a game spinner with a pointer.
fact: In cricket, a spinner is a bowler who makes the ball spin.
fact: A spinner can also be a person who spins wool or thread into yarn.
fact: A fidget spinner is a small toy that spins on your finger.
fact: On a spinner with 4 equal parts, each colour has a 1 in 4 chance of being picked, which is why spinners help you learn probability in maths.
exercise: «A salad spinner flings the water outward and off the leaves.» What is a salad spinner? | A tool that cuts vegetables into thin slices | * A kitchen tool that spins to fling water off wet leaves | A machine that makes salad dressing | A bowl for mixing soup
exercise: In cricket, what is a spinner? | A fielder who catches the ball near the bat | * A bowler who makes the ball spin | A batter who hits the ball very hard | A player who runs between the wickets
exercise: «Use a fidget spinner or small toy in class only if the teacher allows it.» What does this sentence tell you? | You can always use it whenever you like | Toys are banned from school forever | Spinners are only for sport | * You need the teacher's permission first
test: On a spinner with 4 equal parts, what is the chance of landing on one colour? | 4 in 1 | * 1 in 4 | 1 in 10 | 1 in 2
test: What does a spinner mean when someone spins wool or thread? | A pointer on a game board that shows a number | * A person who spins wool or thread into yarn | A bowler who makes the ball turn | A toy that spins on your finger
exam: «The spinner pointed to the red part, so we won the game.» Which meaning fits? | * A game spinner with a pointer | A person who spins wool | A cricket bowler | A fidget toy for your fingers
